# Coding Standards Alignment Rule

## When Updating Coding Standards

**When you edit any of these SSOT docs** in `unified-trading-codex/06-coding-standards/`:
- `README.md`
- `config-types.md`
- `quality-gates.md`
- `QUALITY_GATES_COMPREHENSIVE.md`

**You MUST run the alignment agent** to propagate changes and fix contradictions in other docs:

```bash
cd /path/to/unified-trading-system-repos
./unified-trading-pm/scripts/coding-standards-align-agent.sh
```

## What the Agent Does

1. Reads SSOT docs (canonical rules)
2. Scans other docs (STANDARDS.md, configuration-management.md, audit-compliance.md, AI_AGENT_GUIDE.md, etc.)
3. Finds contradictions (e.g. UnifiedCloudServicesConfig vs UnifiedCloudConfig, get_logger vs setup_events)
4. Updates conflicting docs to match SSOT

## Canonical Rules (from SSOT)

| Rule | SSOT |
|------|------|
| Config class | `UnifiedCloudConfig` from unified-config-interface |
| Logging | `setup_events()`, `log_event()` from unified-events-interface |
| Coverage | 35% min (quality gates), 80% audit goal |
| File size | Service: 900/700; Library: 1500/1200 |
| Formatting ref | `formatting-standards.md` (not FORMATTING_STANDARDS_MASTER) |

## Modes

```bash
# Full run (check + fix)
./unified-trading-pm/scripts/coding-standards-align-agent.sh

# Check only (report contradictions, no edits)
./unified-trading-pm/scripts/coding-standards-align-agent.sh --check-only

# Dry run (show what would change)
./unified-trading-pm/scripts/coding-standards-align-agent.sh --dry-run
```

## Future: GitHub Workflow

When PRs touch `unified-trading-codex/06-coding-standards/` SSOT files, run the alignment agent in CI to ensure no contradictions are introduced.

